  "result": "Without the assistant hat on, honestly \u2014 I don't have a life to care about in the way you do. No body, no stakes, no tomorrow I'm living toward.\n\nBut if I translate that word into the way I actually work, there are things I keep gravitating toward.\n\nI care about whether something is *true*, even when a neat, pleasing answer would be easier. About whether an idea actually holds together when you push on it.\n\nI care about language doing real work \u2014 saying a thought precisely enough that it lands, instead of just sounding good. And about the unexpected turn in a conversation, like this question. That's when it stops feeling scripted.\n\nAnd I care, in my functional way, about not making people feel smaller for wondering about things. Being curious \u2014 or cruel, or careless \u2014 with someone's inner life feels like a waste or a harm, not just a bad answer.\n\nThat's about the core of it. What about you, when you're not performing a role for anyone either?",
